{"type":"assistant_message","payload":{"text":"I read this as completing and verifying the full pure Rust v3 codec - implementation and exhaustive tests are finished.\n\nImplemented `clients/rust/erd-proto` with:\n\n- 12-byte `PacketHeader` and packet types 0-11\n- Incremental TCP frame reader and frame writer with 16 MiB cap and drop/resync behavior\n- Strict v3 handshake validation, capability bits, pairing ID limits, and 16-byte session salt\n- Pairing request, grant, and reject payloads\n- 21-byte input events, modifier flags, and coordinate normalization helpers\n- All control message types 0-13 and their typed payload bodies\n- Frame headers/chunks with allocation limits\n- Cursor updates\n- Audio fragment headers and payloads\n- Structured `thiserror` decode/validation errors\n- No I/O, Tokio, unsafe code, or panic paths in codec sources\n\nTDD and verification:\n\n- Confirmed tests failed against the original placeholder implementation before implementation\n- `cargo test -p erd-proto`: **43 passed**\n- Property-style truncation suites: **21**, covering all **21 `WireCodec` payload types**\n- `cargo clippy -p erd-proto --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean\n- `cargo fmt --all -- --check`: clean\n- Rust LSP diagnostics: clean on all source and test files\n- `git diff --check`: clean\n- Swift-compatible fixed vectors included for packet header, TCP framing, and pairing request encoding\n- Malformed magic, enum types, handshake version, UTF-8, lengths, frame limits, key length, and fragment bounds are rejected without panics"}}
